  {
    "id":539466367,
    "node_id":"R_kgDOICeafw",
    "name":"First-Feature-of-Angular",
    "full_name":"msantos9-dev\/First-Feature-of-Angular",
    "private":false,
    "html_url":"https:\/\/github.com\/msantos9-dev\/First-Feature-of-Angular",
    "description":"Exercise 3 Angular \u2013 Creating your own project Working Code \u2013 40%, Following Requirements \u2013 40%, Error Free \u2013 20% (Submission by github repo) First Feature of Angular (Components, Directives, and Modules) The goal of this exercise is to create the view for user profile, blog list, and book list page Book List Page 1. Create a route for the book module (this should have a \/book route) 2. Create a Book Service under the book\/services folder 3. In the Book Service, we will create an array of books, the Book will have an id:number, name:string, authors:string[], and isbn:string field 4. The Book Service should have a function that will return the array of books 5. Display all the book items in the array in the Book List component coming from the book service (use the Book Item component to display each book instance and use dependency injection) 6. For each item it should have an edit and delete button that will pass the book id to two functions named edit(id:number) and delete(id:number) Blog List Page 1. Create a route for the blog module (this should have a \/blog route) 2. Create a Blog Service under the blog\/services folder 3. In the Blog Service, we will create an array of blogs, the blog will have an id:number, title:string, description:string, author:string, and comments:string[] field (You should create an interface for the Blog object) 4. The Blog Service should have a function that will return the array of blogs 5. Display all the blog items in the array in the Blog List component coming from the blog service (use the Blog Item component to display each blog instance and use dependency injection) 6. For each item it should have an edit and delete button that will pass the blog id to two functions named edit(id:number) and delete(id:number) Profile Page 1. Create a route for the User module (this should have a \/profile route) 2. Create a simple form under the Profiler Component with the following inputs (email, name, bio, active) Shared Components Create the following components Place under \/shared\/components - Header component (header) - Command Bar Component (command-bar) Extra Requirements Add Angular Material in your project",
